m6"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"egZwceqSQn"}],"key":"cxc1S3VrTA"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"s3S8K7mS6Z"}],"key":"PQDNEQKRyG"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"ZqFWAH6VYO"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"cbxSUEYqmd"}],"key":"jZ3H01X82s"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"bjIinYF25E"}],"key":"RYHwCDn8JJ"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.lock-files.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"AflkMR0u7f"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"MFtsEGdGfE"}],"key":"RHvwc2kYCt"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"XwNUvrer83"}],"key":"rN9Rk1wwYx"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"UtcX4KTodW"}],"key":"BBtUu7EcmL"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"LlCFUxk9JU"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"jWOISuMPQz"}],"key":"QNXvijmkBc"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"hxMYbdlH8B"}],"key":"FTBiO9kxbT"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jet-lag.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"FmhriZCn1D"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"Rs3uWLHdIW"}],"key":"fzMs1jlkrb"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"Cx5PhCQLqn"}],"key":"xJjY8NaEdj"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"jD0UKUG8RJ"}],"key":"Wr6JtIxTNj"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"oAKD2ufJt9"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"mpE6PfrR4G"}],"key":"uwadYubBcx"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"GFBF9KgclG"}],"key":"h8CkJTQofJ"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.fund-systems-not-developmend.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"SSbAjXT5El"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"CwFUPPc4eK"}],"key":"OuyMKc67Fc"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"JZEX5vr2g4"}],"key":"yGT6YprXfK"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"SUkABoTaMi"}],"key":"xxFbygFLff"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"bTd41kMMRe"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"xYNb9zUgUw"}],"key":"t1BvcFAFFE"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"D6LGcOetuC"}],"key":"Ri7XCuD6Ih"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.more-contributors.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"z04xYSGkwF"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"iyFw2Wt6Hv"}],"key":"sIc9ABIIfl"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"DrJg5s3qnP"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"R9Buzn9KiT"}],"key":"OCA6KfFfl8"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"KuJ2HpyeUX"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"h0ZYjXRrs9"}],"key":"QWb2FB6bQ8"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"SCZIRsczNk"}],"key":"wCku3AVlm7"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"INYcJmX9fa"}],"key":"ul3rP3qoXE"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"BauNbu21ft"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"Y5J3xqwOgw"}],"key":"ci19yHmw2v"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"rc0GGeQzPj"}],"key":"CR2gJjjNfW"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jupyter-org-structure.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"fS2HOJIiLj"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"ZH92h74574"}],"key":"Q3HWY8Jrid"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"MkBUkYczzy"}],"key":"gcjtM8e9un"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"XY0v1qBKXO"}],"key":"lZKy2upoYd"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"IiNMEOQVZm"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"JGgoUL76GI"}],"key":"WQZxjHeA4f"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"wlGJCMDIk1"}],"key":"dlyQRHgTaT"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.os-support.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"l6JZicWx5U"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"EsQ6HXUpz6"}],"key":"gkCrhcADou"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"CtdsPX0Xbh"}],"key":"ogmtDCry3t"},{"type":"f